# Seeds for failure cases proptest has generated in the past. It is
# automatically read and these particular cases re-run before any
# novel cases are generated.
#
# It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
# everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases.
#
# Trimmed by hand to one seed per distinct finding. What each one caught:
#
#   "\r\n"                     — a message that is only the separator. The
#                                leading CRLF was parsed as a nameless field and
#                                carried above everything the rewrite wrote,
#                                cutting the header block off before it started.
#                                Fixed in rewrite::headers::find_separator.
#   "Smith, Jane"              — a display name containing a comma, written
#                                unquoted, turns one mailbox into two; the second
#                                pass then read the display name as "Smith".
#                                Fixed by quoting substituted values at the
#                                substitution boundary
#                                (rewrite::template::Template::render_header).
#   minimal From:-only message — a harness fault, not a code fault: the two
#                                passes were being compared after stripping one
#                                Received: from each, when only the second pass
#                                has one to spare. Kept because it is the
#                                smallest input the properties run on.
cc d34eda30172306590424f103473607147b5a58cd390cd79843523c2f569c15f3 # shrinks to m = "\r\n"
cc cf595d3d4a2a5496d75871987f069c6a74176fb64eba5b766529f6aa15bd247b # shrinks to m = "From: \"Smith, Jane\" <jane@oldbrand.com>\r\n\r\n"
cc f3408c04e4b47ff36e7eb5bb984a601fd48d9b3d2f8aa00b1ef75cfafe64701d # shrinks to m = "From: jane@oldbrand.com\r\n\r\n"
